      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "comment before Lane_Agent",
      "prov:value": "`roles.json` matches a lane to a role by name, and that indirection is how one role ended up carrying five aliases because five diagrams each named the same lane differently. \"Contributor\" is what this lane IS in this process; `user` is the declared role performing it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "library/processes/content-acquisition.bpmn#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "task A_PointToUpload",
      "prov:value": "Composed from the declaration, never written by hand. The queue is declared with INSTANCE scope, so its declared path is missing the segment a repository-relative forge URL needs: /upload/main/uploads is a 404 and /upload/main/cat-harness/uploads is not, verified against GitHub 2026-09-20. Every failure is named — no origin remote, a non-GitHub forge, a declared-but-absent queue — because a URL is believed, and somebody sent to a wrong one cannot tell it from an empty directory. On failure, fall back to the conversation. Uses `scripts/upload-url.ts`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
